From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:30:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hwcontext_vaapi: accept GR1616 chroma for P010 and P012 DRM
 import

hwcontext_vulkan exports the chroma plane of P010 and P012 frames,
VK_FORMAT_R16G16_UNORM, as DRM_FORMAT_GR1616: vulkan_fmt_to_drm()
returns the first match in vulkan_drm_format_map, which lists GR1616
before RG1616. The VAAPI DRM import table only knows RG1616 for these
formats, so mapping a 10- or 12-bit Vulkan frame to VAAPI fails with
"DRM format not supported by VAAPI".

GR1616 carries R in the low 16 bits, which is the memory order of a
Vulkan R16G16 plane. Accept it next to RG1616, as the table already
does with GR88 and RG88 for NV12, which Vulkan exports as GR88.

Tested on an Intel Arc A380 (iHD 26.3.5) and an AMD Radeon 610M
(radeonsi), in a build that also waited on the CPU before the map
instead of attaching a sync file: Vulkan P010 frames map to VAAPI, read
back bit-exact and encode with hevc_vaapi Main10. Without this change
the map is refused on both. P012 was not tested.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
---
 libavutil/hwcontext_vaapi.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavutil/hwcontext_vaapi.c b/libavutil/hwcontext_vaapi.c
index 98130f9fb1f230ee369393fcee1024b89b7466f3..d80e1409e29d5f0e48f4ee704a1cec8b7c037f25 100644
--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_vaapi.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_vaapi.c
@@ -1065,9 +1065,11 @@ static const struct {
     DRM_MAP(NV12, 1, DRM_FORMAT_NV12),
 #if defined(VA_FOURCC_P010) && defined(DRM_FORMAT_R16)
     DRM_MAP(P010, 2, DRM_FORMAT_R16, DRM_FORMAT_RG1616),
+    DRM_MAP(P010, 2, DRM_FORMAT_R16, DRM_FORMAT_GR1616),
 #endif
 #if defined(VA_FOURCC_P012) && defined(DRM_FORMAT_R16)
     DRM_MAP(P012, 2, DRM_FORMAT_R16, DRM_FORMAT_RG1616),
+    DRM_MAP(P012, 2, DRM_FORMAT_R16, DRM_FORMAT_GR1616),
 #endif
     DRM_MAP(BGRA, 1, DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888),
     DRM_MAP(BGRX, 1, DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888),
